+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// Portable HIP reference path - see scripts/rocm/patches/0001-*.patch.
+//
+// The CUDA original hands raw F32 register bits to
+// `mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k8.row.col.f32.tf32.tf32.f32`, so each product is
+// formed from operands truncated to tf32 (10 explicit mantissa bits) and
+// accumulated in F32. AMD matrix intrinsics do not accept NVIDIA fragment
+// layouts, and the rollout plan requires a correct reference path before any
+// optimisation, so this computes the same quantity directly.
+//
+// Preserved deliberately: tf32 operand truncation, F32 accumulation, the
+// per-head ReLU, the ordered head addition, the optional F32 block bias, the
+// finite 1e9 F32 bias on the incomplete tail block, the reference's +0 bias on
+// full blocks, the write range [0, n_kv), the spare-row tolerance and the
+// invalid-count early exit.
+//
+// Differs deliberately, and stated rather than hidden: the reduction is one
+// sequential F32 sum over d, where the original splits d across two warps and
+// each tensor-core step sums an 8-wide slice internally. Bitwise agreement with
+// NVIDIA is therefore not claimed and is not required by the plan. The measured
+// deviation from a float64 reference is bounded and checked by
+// tests/rocm/qsa_score_parity.cpp.
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+// tf32 keeps the top 19 bits of an F32; the low 13 mantissa bits are what the
+// tensor core never sees when raw F32 registers are passed to it.
+__device__ __forceinline__ float strata_tf32_as_mma_sees_it(float x) {
+    return __uint_as_float(__float_as_uint(x) & 0xFFFFE000u);
 }
